        "original_id": "ecdd7a71-90ca-5b72-b11f-4dfaeea1e0b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Withers, Donna Weiss, Jackie DeShannon, Bette Davis\n- Songs: Bette Davis Eyes, Just the Two of Us\n- Albums: Winelight\n- Awards: Grammy Awards\n- Charts: Billboard Hot 100, Vatican City Top 40\n\nFacts:\n- An edited version of “Bette Davis Eyes” from the album “Winelight” reached number two on the Billboard Hot 100.\n- The chunk describes “Bette Davis Eyes” as a Grammy Award-winning hit associated with Bill Withers.\n- “Just the Two of Us” was written and composed by Donna Weiss and Jackie DeShannon.\n- “Just the Two of Us” spent nine weeks at number one in the Vatican City Top 40.\n- “Just the Two of Us” was the song ahead of “Bette Davis Eyes” on the Billboard Hot 100.",
